error[E1004]: this stores a value from `item`'s region into `holder`'s region — parameter regions are independent by default
 --> mem:///main.lu:4:5
  |
3 | fn stash(mut holder: Holder, take item: Item) {
  |              ------ the container lives in `holder`'s region
  |                                   ---- the value arrives here, in `item`'s region
4 |     holder.item = item
  |     ^^^^^^^^^^^ the store that would tie the two regions together
  |
  = note: each parameter's data lives in its own (generalized) region — the Cyclone default that
    keeps signatures annotation-free. A signature surface for declaring two parameters share
    a region is planned; today, `copy` the value into its container's region, or restructure
    so the allocation happens alongside the container.
